.TH FINALTREE 1 "2026-11-28" "finaltree 0.21.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
finaltree \- working-tree provenance fingerprinter and gate-log stamper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B finaltree fingerprint
.RB [ \-\-generated
.I PATTERN
.RI ... ]
.I ROOT
.br
.B finaltree stamp
.I ROOT
.B \-\-log
.I PATH
.RB [ \-\-generated
.I PATTERN
.RI ... ]
.B \-\-
.I COMMAND
.RI [ ARG ... ]
.br
.B finaltree verify
.I LOG ROOT
.RB [ \-\-generated
.I PATTERN
.RI ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B finaltree
computes a canonical SHA-256 fingerprint of a local Git working tree
.RB ( HEAD ,
tracked working-tree and index blobs, untracked files, declared
.B \-\-generated
artifacts, ignored files, modes, and recursive submodules), prefixes every
line of gate output with that digest in
.BR finaltree\-stamped\-log/1 ,
records an unkeyed SHA-256
.B evidence\-digest
over the command, exit code, and output lines, and verifies merge-candidate
provenance.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B fingerprint
Print canonical
.B finaltree\-fingerprint/1
JSON for
.I ROOT
to standard output.
.TP
.B stamp
Fingerprint
.IR ROOT ,
execute
.I COMMAND
inside
.IR ROOT ,
write the stamped log to
.BR \-\-log ,
and exit with the gate command's exit status. Keep
.B \-\-log
and compiler scratch directories outside
.IR ROOT .
.TP
.B verify
Validate log formatting and
.BR evidence\-digest ,
recompute the fingerprint of
.IR ROOT ,
and print
.B match
(exit 0) or
.B mismatch
with member-level differences (exit 1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Fingerprint succeeded, stamped gate exited 0, or verify matched.
.TP
.B 1
Verify detected working-tree differences (or stamped gate exited 1).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, malformed or truncated log, or unreadable/unborn repository
refusal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/tmp/gate-target finaltree stamp . --log /tmp/gate.stamped.log -- cargo test --locked
finaltree verify /tmp/gate.stamped.log . && grep -qx 'exit-code 0' /tmp/gate.stamped.log
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://david-engelmann.github.io/finaltree/
.SH AUTHORS
David Engelmann
